RESULT: Domain-controller discovery from VM 102 is fully functional. nltest resolves DC01 with the complete expected capability flag set (PDC GC DS LDAP KDC WRITABLE). The _ldap._tcp.dc._msdcs SRV record resolves correctly to dc01.district.local:389.

This closed a real gap in prior testing: earlier checks had only proven a plain A-record lookup of district.local worked. AD-aware installers use SRV-based DC locator, a different mechanism entirely -- and domain join can succeed via a more tolerant discovery path than an installer's validation uses, so "the domain join worked" was never proof this would. Tested rather than assumed; both came back clean, ruling out DNS/discovery as the cause of the Entra Connect wizard failure.

Filing note: the SRV response was trimmed of repeated per-record serialization boilerplate (CharacterSet, Section, DataLength, QueryType) for legibility. All values shown are unedited.
